      <scopecontent id="aspace_b14254a2c99cb29bb66cdd9a55e1b349">
         <head>Scope and Contents</head>
         <p>The collection contains typewritten and handwritten letters by bookplate collector William R. A. Hays to bookplate artist Frederick C. Blank. Correspondence relates to all aspects of bookplate collecting and mentions many prominent designers and engravers of bookplates.</p>
      </scopecontent>
      <arrangement id="aspace_23a9e85ec9b10b60622f33933a149d1c">
         <head>Arrangement</head>
         <p>Organized chronologically.</p>
      </arrangement>
      <bioghist id="aspace_938ba1fabff0e347c71df82d0bf03fb8">
         <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
         <p>William R. A. Hays was a broker, lawyer, and noted bookplate collector from Cleveland, Ohio. Frederck Charles Blank (1866-1942) was born in Rockville, Connecticut, and studied engraving under Frederick Leigh in Hartford Connecticut. He worked as an engraver for the Brooklyn Watch Case Company, the John Robbins Manufacturing Company, and the Gillette Safety Razor Company. He also designed bookplates beginning in 1917, and won international awards from the Bookplate Association in 1929 and 1932.</p>
      </bioghist>
